course: dictionary
lesson: 12309
title: One word, several groups
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Corps» is one of them. Its meaning depends on the words around it, so read the context to find out which meaning the writer wants. «The soldiers in the Royal Army Medical Corps cared for the wounded.» Here a corps is a part of an army with a special job.
explain: «The press corps waited outside the palace for news.» The clue is the word press, which tells you about news and reporters. So a corps can also be a group of people who work together on a special task. In a ballet, «The corps de ballet danced behind the star.» Here the clue is ballet, and the corps is the group of dancers, not the soloists.
explain: Use the context clues first, then check by putting your meaning into the sentence. If the meaning fits every time, you have found the right one.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Corps» has three main meanings: a part of an army with a special job, a group working together on a special task, and the group of dancers in a ballet.
fact: «Corps» is spoken as «kor»: the final s and p are silent.
fact: The plural of «corps» is also «corps», so you write the same word for one group or many.
fact: Examples: «Marine Corps», «Peace Corps», «diplomatic corps», and «corps de ballet».
exercise: «The soldiers in the medical corps helped the injured people.» What is a corps in this sentence? | *A part of an army with a special job | A kind of hospital bed | A type of dance | A large brown bird
exercise: «The corps de ballet danced together behind the star.» Who are the corps de ballet? | The one main dancer who does all the solo parts | *A group of dancers who dance together, not the soloists | The people who sell the tickets | The orchestra playing the music
exercise: Mia says the plural of corps is corpses. What is the plural of corps? | corpuses | corpi | corpses | *corps
test: «The press corps asked the minister questions after the meeting.» What is the press corps? | *A group of reporters who report the news | A kind of army tent | A group of dancers in a ballet | A bunch of flowers
test: Which one names a group of people who work together on a special task? | Royal Navy ship | *Peace Corps | Pea soup | Corpse
exam: Which phrase names a part of an army with a special job? | *Marine Corps | Press corps | Corps de ballet | Garden shed
